<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17184" root="رى" body-key="r">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَيَيْتُ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَيَّيْتُ</span></b> , inf. n. of the former <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَىٌّ</span>
and of the latter <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَرْيِيَةٌ</span>, are both of them verbs
relating to <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الرَّايَةُ</span>: (T:) you say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الرَّايَةَ</span> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَيَّيْتُ</span></b> 
[and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَيَيْتُهَا</span>] <i>I made the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَايَة</span> [q. v.]: (M, TA:)
the imperative of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَيَيْتُ</span> is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِرْيَهْ</span>, and that of ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَيَّيْتُ</span></b> 
is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَيِّهْ</span>: and the pass. part. ns. are ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَرْيِىٌّ</span></b>  and
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرَىٌّ</span></b> , each applied to a banner. (T.)

